WEBVTT

00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:15,630
I recently got another breast thermogram done. It's my first sense the full body was done at the

00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:20,430
clinic two years ago. The full thermogram two years ago did not show any activity in the breast.

00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:26,030
I was told that this was because frequently my type of cancer will not show up on a thermogram.

00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:32,830
Yes, that's true. This most recent thermogram, however, did show activity at the tumor site.

00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:39,710
Is this necessarily vascular activity that is feeding the cancer? Is it possible that it's

00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:50,290
inflammation related to topically applying frankincense at DMSO every day? So what will show up on

00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:57,570
a thermogram is metabolic activity. So metabolic activity can be cell growth and replication

00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:02,530
cells. That's going to increase metabolic activity and in any increase in metabolic activity

00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:06,770
is going to increase heat. So what a thermogram is reading is heat.

00:01:07,490 --> 00:01:16,690
Now, thermograms have negatives to them too. So some breast cancers don't replicate quickly,

00:01:16,690 --> 00:01:23,410
therefore don't produce a lot of heat. Some cancers, the breast cancer, are too deep

00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:28,850
to actually have the heat be expressed on the surface of the body, therefore you can't really see

00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:36,370
about a thermogram. So it's not highly beneficial for a colon cancer or something.

00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:46,930
But increased vascularization could increase heat. So that's a possibility.

00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:57,010
But certainly doing anything topical on the skin is going to increase heat. So in this case,

00:01:57,010 --> 00:02:02,690
I would say if you have been applying frankincense at DMSO on a daily basis,

00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:10,450
I'd say you got about 99% chance. That's what it's fun. Now, if you really wanted to test it,

00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:17,970
you'd stop doing that for a period of time. And it's in a German period of time because you don't

00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:22,930
know how long that that's going to take, but at least two weeks before doing it on a thermogram.

00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:31,890
But that would be one way to test it.

